<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56258" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυσ-τός</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυτός</span></b>  (as Inscrr.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>burnt, red-hot</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυτὸν μοχλόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Cyc.</u>
					633
				</span></i>
			 (Scal.for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ τὸν</span>):
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυστόν, τό</span>, <i>burnt-offering for the dead</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυτόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			; <i>whole burnt-offering</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγοντι τὸμ βοῦν καὶ τὸγ καυτόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					1025.31
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Cos</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρὴν
				καυτός</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1027.9
			</span></i> (ibid.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>capable of being burnt</i>, opp.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκαυστος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				387a17
			</span></i>, al.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυστικός</span>: 
				Comp.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότερος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Ign.</u>
				72
			</span></i>.</div>
